# Design document sync

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

`docs/explanation/architecture.md` describes the system as it is built today: data flow, deployment, components, runtime image, pipeline processes, archive layout, database and metrics, the `host_data.type` contract, Valkey roles, web/API layers, and security/config. Per-service facts (images, limits, mounts, commands) live in `docs/reference/compose-services.md`. When a change would make any statement there wrong, update the doc **in the same task**. Write it per `docs-current-state-only.mdc` (current behaviour only, no changelog text).

## Trigger conditions

| Change | Section to check |
|--------|-----------------------------|
| Service added, removed or renamed in `docker-compose.defaults.yaml` / `docker-compose.yaml.example` / `docker-compose.pg15-primary.yaml`; image, network or volume role changed | architecture: Data flow, Deployment; compose-services: the service's section |
| Version pin changed in `services-conf/*.Dockerfile`, `pyproject.toml`, `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/package.json` (PostgreSQL, TimescaleDB, Python, Django, React/Next, nginx, Valkey, RabbitMQ, Codon, zstd) when the doc names that version | Wherever the version is cited (compose-services image sections, architecture Runtime image) |
| Pipeline program added/removed/renamed in `services-conf/supervisord.conf`, or a long-running process's role changes (`listend`, `sync_timedb`, `update_metrics`, rsync, syslog) | architecture: Runtime processes; compose-services: Supervisord programs |
| Top-level package moved/added under `hpcperfstats/`, or `hpcperfstats-tools/` scope changes | architecture: Python packages |
| Archive directory layout or file naming written by `listend` / `sync_timedb` | architecture: Archive layout |
| Core tables, hypertables, or metrics storage changed (Django models / migrations under `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/`) | architecture: Database and metrics |
| `host_data.type` names or monitor collector set changed (`monitor-analysis-architecture-sync.mdc`) | architecture: Monitor, Monitor and analysis contract |
| Valkey key namespaces or Valkey roles changed | architecture: Valkey roles |
| Web/API layering changed (Django API, OpenAPI/Orval, SPA, nginx allowlist) | architecture: Web application and APIs |
| Auth, secrets, INI or operations model changed | architecture: Security, configuration and operations |
| A doc linked from the pages is added, moved or removed | Inbound links (layout test) |

## Required actions

1. Update every affected section; copy names and versions from code, not memory.
2. Keep links valid (`hpcperfstats/tests/test_docs_layout.py` checks them).
3. Keep each fact on one page and link to it; cross-check `docs/tutorials/install-hpcperfstats.md`, `docs/reference/pipeline-configuration.md` and `docs/explanation/pipeline-concurrency.md` for the same fact; they must agree.

## Overlap

- `docs-current-state-only.mdc` — writing style for this doc.
- `monitor-analysis-architecture-sync.mdc` — `host_data.type` contract details.
- `readme-installation-sync.mdc` — operator setup facts in the install tutorial.
